          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Lie group cohomology
            generalizes the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            from
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
          %p
            From the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nPOV"} nPOV
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a Lie group, its cohomology is the intrinsic cohomology of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"}
                Smth
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                Grpd
          %p
            In the literature one finds a sequence of definitions that approach this intrisic topos-theoretic definition. This is discussed below. For a detailed discussion of the relation of this to the intrinsic topos-theoretic definition see the section
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lie+infinity-groupoid#CohomologyOfLieGroups"} Cohomology of Lie groups
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} ∞-Lie groupoid
          %h3#structured_group_cohomology Structured group cohomology
          %p
            If the groups in question are not
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            but groups with extra structure, such as
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
          %p
            In parts of the literature cohomology of structured groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is defined in direct generalization of the formulas above as homotopy classes of morphisms from the simplicial object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mo *
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left(
                  \\cdots G \times G\stackrel{\to}{\stackrel{\to}{\to}}G \stackrel{\to}{\to} *
                  \\right)
          %p
            to a simplicial object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N (\mathbf{B}^n A)
          %p
            This is what is described above. But this does
            %strong not
            in general give the right answer for structured groups:
          %p
            namely
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            is really about homotopy classes of maps in the suitable ambient
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-space"} derived hom-space
            between these objects.
          %p
            But this changes as we consider groups with extra structure. For a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mo *
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left(
                  \\cdots G \times G\stackrel{\to}{\stackrel{\to}{\to}}G \stackrel{\to}{\to} *
                  \\right)
          %p
            has to be considered as an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} Lie ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            %strong not
            both cofibrant and fibrant. To that extent plain morphisms out of this object do
            %strong not
            compute the correct
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-space"} derived hom-space
          %h3#TopologicalGroupCohomology Topological group cohomology
          %p In
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"}> Jim Stasheff
              ,
              %em Continuous cohomology of groups and classifying spaces
              Bull. Amer. Math. Soc. Volume 84, Number 4 (1978), 513-530 (
              %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/DPubS?service=UI&version=1.0&verb=Display&handle=euclid.bams/1183540920"}> web
              )
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            \-cocycles on a topological group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            with valzues in a topological abelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            are considered as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mrow
                      %mo ×
                      %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G^{\times n}\to A
            (p. 3 ). (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+cohomology"}> continuous cohomology
            ”)
          %p
            A definition in terms of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} Ext-functor
          %ul
            %li
              David Wigner,
              %em Algebraic cohomology of topological groups
              Transactions of the American Mathematical Society, volume 178 (1973)(
              %a{:href => "http://egg.epfl.ch/~nmonod/bonn/Wigner_1973.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p A classical reference that considers the cohomology of Lie groups as topological spaces is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Armand+Borel"}> Armand Borel
              ,
              %em Homology and cohomology of compact connected Lie groups
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC1063923/pdf/pnas01596-0040.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p A corrected definition of topological group cohomology has been given by Segal
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
                ,
                %em Cohomology of topological groups
                In Symposia Mathematica, Vol. IV (INDAM, Rome, 1968/69), pages 377{387. Academic Press, London, (1970).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
                ,
                %em A classifying space of a topological group in the sense of Gel’fand-Fuks. Funkcional. Anal. i Prilozen., 9(2):48{50, (1975).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            an abelian Lie group, write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi naive
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi smooth
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mrow
                      %mo ×
                      %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H_{naive}^n(G,A) = \{smooth G^{\times n } \to A\}/_\sim
          %p
            for the naive notion of cohomology on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            A refined definition of Lie group cohomology, denoted
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi diff
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n_{diff}(G,A)
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Brylinski"} Brylinski
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Blanc"} Blanc
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Shommer-Pries"} Schommer-Pries
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Brylinski)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+space"}> paracompact
              ) and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              an abelian Lie group.
            %p
              For eack
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              we can pick a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+cover"} good open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msubsup
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U^{k}_{i} \to G^{\times_k}| i \in I_k\}
              such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the index sets arrange themselves into a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi I
                          %mo :
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ↦
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I : [k] \mapsto I_k
              %li
                %p
                  and for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_j(U^k_i)
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_j(U^k_i)
                  the images of the face and degeneracy maps of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi G
                          %mrow
                            %mo ×
                            %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G^{\times\bullet}
                  we have
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msubsup
                          %mi U
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        d_j(U^k_i) \subset U^{k-1}_{d_j(i)}
                %p and
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msubsup
                          %mi U
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi s
                              %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        s_j(U^k_i) \subset U^{k+1}_{s_j(i)}
                        \\,.
            %p
              Then the
              %strong differentiable group cohomology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              with coefficients in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is the cohomology of the total complex of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech
              double complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mo •
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty( U^{\bullet}_{i_0, \cdots, i_\bullet} , A)
              whose differentials are the alternating sums of the face maps of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G^{\times_\bullet}
              and of the
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi diff
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mi Tot
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mo •
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^n_{diff}(G,A) := H^n Tot C^\infty( U^{\bullet}_{i_0, \cdots, i_\bullet} , A)
          %p
            This is definition 1.1 in (
            %a{:href => "#Brylinski"}> Brylinski
            )
          %p
            As discussed there, this is equivalent to other definitions, notably to a definition given earlier by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"} Graeme Segal
          %p There is an evident morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi naive
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi diff
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^n_{naive}(G,A) \to H^n_{diff}(G,A)
          %p obtained by pulling back a globally defined smooth cocycle to a cover.
          %p
            At
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} ∞-Lie groupoid
            it is discussed that there is a further refinement
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi diff
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^n_{diff}(G,A) \to H^n(\mathbf{B}G,A)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where on the right we have the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} intrinsic cohomology
            of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} ∞-Lie groupoid
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          %p
            From now on, for definiteness by a
            %em Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            we mean (following
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0011/0011069v1.pdf#page=3"} Bry, page3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+space"} paracompact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frechet+manifold"} Frechet manifold
            equipped with a group structure such that the product and the inverse maps are smooth, and there is an everywhere defined exponential map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} exp : \mathfrak{g} \to G
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If the coefficient Lie group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} topological vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi smooth
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mrow
                        %mo ×
                        %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n(G,A) = \{smooth G^{\times n} \to A\}/_\sim
              coincides with the correct Lie group cohomology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mi top
                    %mo .
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi vect
                    %mo .
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi space
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi naive
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi diff
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (A top.\;vect.\;space) \Rightarrow
                    (H^n_{naive}(G,A) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} H^n_{diff}(G,A) )
                    \\,.
            %p
              If the coefficient Lie group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is discrete, then Lie group cohomology coindices with the topological cohomology of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mi discrete
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (A discrete) \Rightarrow
                    (H^n(G,A) \simeq H^n(\mathcal{B}G), A)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              This is
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0011/0011069v1.pdf#page=4"} Bry, prop. 1.3
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0011/0011069v1.pdf#page=5"} Bry, lemma 1.5
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi diff
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^2_{diff}(G,A)
              classifies central
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extension"} extensions of Lie groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi π
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \to \hat G \stackrel{\pi}{\to} G
            %p
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo :
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : \hat G \to G
              is a locally trivial smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal
              = succeed "-fibration." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              The image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi naive
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi diff
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^2_{naive}(G,A) \to H^2_{diff}(G,A)
              consists of those central extensions for which is bundle is trivial.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              This is
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0011/0011069v1.pdf#page=4"} Bry, prop. 1.6
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0011/0011069v1.pdf#page=5"} Bry, lemma 1.5
          %h3#SequenceDiffCohomology Long sequence in differential cohomology
          %p
            For the purpose of this section we specifically conceive Lie group cohomology inside the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9ELieGrpd"} ∞LieGrpd
            of
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} ∞-Lie groupoid
          %p
            This is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} local (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
            and therefore it admits
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} differential cohomology in an (∞,1)-topos
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+an+(%E2%88%9E%2C1)-topos#DiffCohWithGroupalCoeffs"} differential fiber sequence
            we have for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^{n} U(1)
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} circle n+1-group
            a long sequence in cohomology
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi diff
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi G
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi dR
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \to H^n_{diff}(G, (1))\to H^n_G(G,U(1)) \to H_{dR, G}^{n+1}(G) \to
                  \\cdots
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_G(G,-)
            denotes
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi G
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^n_G(G,A) := \pi_0 \mathbf{H}(\mathbf{B}G, \mathbf{B}^n A)
          %p and so on.
          %p
            The point to note is that we may identify
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            inside
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi dR
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n_{dR,G}(G)
            and may therefore regard the map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi G
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi dR
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^n_G(G,U(1)) \to H_{dR, G}^{n+1}(G)
          %p
            as the differentiation map that take a smooth group cocycle to a Lie algebra cocycle. This morphism operates by putting constructing a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle n-bundle with connection
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            and then computing its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            forms.
          %p
            %strong Example
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+algebra"} semisimple Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            its simply connected Lie group, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 3
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G \to \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)
            be the group cocycle that classifies the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} string 2-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi dR
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^3_{dR,G}(G)
            is the curvature of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+circle+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons circle 3-bundle
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                the form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi θ
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi θ
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi θ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle \theta\wedge \theta \wedge \theta \rangle
                obtained by feeding the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                into the canoical Lie algebra cocycle that is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+element"} in transtression
                with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+form"} Killing form
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            %li
              %p
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ×
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \times G
                something like
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mi θ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ∧
                        %msub
                          %mi θ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle \theta_1 \wedge \theta_2\rangle
          %p (…)
          %h3#relation_to_intrinsic_cohomology_of_smooth_groupoids
            Relation to intrinsic cohomology of smooth
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            We may naturally regard a Lie group as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
            = succeed "-theoretic" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p For
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  either a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  the additive Lie group of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℝ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
                  or the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi Z
                        %mo =
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}/Z = U(1)
            %p
              the intrinsic cohomology of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
              coincides with the refined
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group+cohomology"} Lie group cohomology
              of (
              %a{:href => "#Segal"}> Segal
              )(
              %a{:href => "#Brylinski"}> Brylinski
              )
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi Smooth
                        %mn ∞
                        %mi Grpd
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi diffr
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^n_{Smooth\infty Grpd}(\mathbf{B}G, A) \simeq H^n_{diffr}(G,A)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is discussed in detail at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            and proven at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SynthDiff%E2%88%9EGrpd"} SynthDiff∞Grpd
          %h3#relation_to_lie_algebra_cohomology Relation to Lie algebra cohomology
          %p
            The content of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/van+Est+isomorphism"} van Est isomorphism
            is that the canonical comparison map from Lie group cohomology to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            (by
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiation"} differentiation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            whenever the Lie group is sufficiently connected.
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+group+cohomology"}> nonabelian group cohomology
                    ,
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+cohomology"} groupoid cohomology
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group+cohomology"} ∞-group cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extension"} group extension
            %li
              %p
                %strong Lie group cohomology
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid+cohomology"} ∞-Lie groupoid cohomology
          %h2#references References
          %p A textbook account of standard material is in chapter V in vol III of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Werner+Greub"}> Werner Greub
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Halperin"} Stephen Halperin
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ray+Vanstone"} Ray Vanstone
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Connections%2C+Curvature%2C+and+Cohomology"} Connections, Curvature, and Cohomology
              Academic Press (1973)
          %p
            The definition of the refined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            cohomology in terms of degreewise
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            was given in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Cohomology of topological groups
              %p
                Symposia mathematica. Volume IV, pp. 377–387. Convegni del Dicembre del 1968 e del Marzo del 1969. Istituto Nazionale di Alta Matematica, Roma. Academic Press, London–New York, 1970. iv+542 pp.
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://dmitripavlov.org/scans/segal-cohomology-of-topological-groups.pdf"} PDF
          %p
            It was later rediscovered for
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
          %ul
            %li#Brylinski
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Luc+Brylinski"}> Jean-Luc Brylinski
              ,
              %em Differentiable Cohomology of Gauge Groups
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0011069"}> arXiv
              )
          %p following
          %ul
            %li#Blanc
              P. Blanc,
              %em Cohomologie différentiable et changement de groupes, Astérisque vol. 124-125 (1985), pp. 113-130
          %p Further discussion:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Friedrich+Wagemann"}> Friedrich Wagemann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Wockel"} Christoph Wockel
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Cocycle Model for Topological and Lie Group Cohomology
              %strong 367
              3 (2015) 1871-1909 (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1110.3304"}> arXiv:1110.3304
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/24513021"} jstor:24513021
          %p Relevant background on the theory of abelian sheaf cohomology on simplicial spaces is at the beginning of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
              ,
              %em Théorie de Hodge: III
              Publication mathétematique de l’I.H.E.S, tome 44 (1974), p. 5-77 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=PMIHES_1974__44__5_0"}> numdam
              )
          %p More discussion of Lie group cohomology along these lines is in
          %ul#Schommer-Pries
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Schommer-Pries"}> Chris Schommer-Pries
              ,
              %em A finite-dimensional String 2-group
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0911.2483"}> arXiv:0911.2483
              )
          %p
            A discussion of the relation between
            %em local
            Lie group cohomology and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              S. Świerczkowski,
              %em Cohomology of group germs and Lie algebras
              Pacific Journal of Mathematics, Volume 39, Number 2 (1971), 471-482. (
              %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/DPubS/Repository/1.0/Disseminate?view=body&id=pdf_1&handle=euclid.pjm/1102969572"}> pdf
              )
